{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>A fifth to Pharaoh, etc.</b> One may offer the clever explanation that first of all Pharaoh takes a fifth of the seed, and it works out that in the remaining four portions there remains enough for seed for the field, and they go out scot-free; even so, the fifth for Pharaoh is not diminished. After that, ״ולזרע השדה״ — and they would set aside the seed for the field first, and afterward they themselves take all that remains, whether little or much." "<b>And the reason</b> He said <b>ולאכל לטפכם</b> and did not include them under ״לאשר בבתיכם״, is so that the children's portion would be increased relative to the surplus share; therefore He said ״ולאכל לטפכם״."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:49:35.155663704Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}